# Adopters whose own test suites gate a release — read by tools/adopters-gate.raku.
#
# Only the address and a pinned commit live here. The code stays in its own
# repository and is cloned into a cache when the gate runs.
#
#   adopter NAME URL COMMIT ENTRY TEST-BIN-VAR
#       ENTRY is the program their CI compiles with `--aot --standalone`;
#       TEST-BIN-VAR is the variable that points their suite at that file.
#   known   NAME WHAT REASON…
#       a failure that is expected: WHAT is a test file (t/…), `build`
#       (the standalone compile), `*` (every file and the build), or several
#       of those joined by commas.
#
# Move a pin only after running the gate with --head on the new commit. When a
# `known` line starts passing, the gate says so: delete the line.

adopter 321 https://github.com/nige123/cli.321.do 39ddf8a8957d54b3dd12e74e86cf9ad086a93560 bin/321 DO321_TEST_BIN
# Behind Shape.rakumod (lines 47, 54, 64, 138) there are four more of the same
# kind, each behaving the same way on Rakudo, found with --dirty on a patched
# checkout (2026-10-03): `$a && (…){$k}:exists` (Trust.rakumod:221),
# `without … else` (Run.rakumod:260, 464), `try $p.in.close` sinking a failed
# Proc (Run.rakumod:534, t/lib/Do321Test.rakumod:68), and Arrays assigned into
# %args before `Summary.new(|%args)`, which itemizes them so `@.denials` gets
# one element (Adapter.rakumod:719, 726). With all five fixed, 886 of 887 pass;
# t/03-trust test 38 links to /etc/hostname, which this macOS lacks.
known   321 build,t/01-protocol.rakutest,t/02-digest.rakutest,t/03-trust.rakutest,t/04-tool.rakutest,t/05-adapter.rakutest,t/06-run.rakutest,t/07-run-tool.rakutest,t/08-claudecode.rakutest,t/09-wire.rakutest,t/10-cli.rakutest,t/11-hooks.rakutest,t/12-iz4-policy.rakutest lib/Do321/Shape.rakumod:47 passes a lone Pair, `(k => 'v')`, to `@fields`; Rakudo refuses it too (needs a trailing comma). Raku++ v4.0.1, their pin, accepted it.

adopter iz4 https://github.com/nige123/cli.iz4.you 2eb86ab720658a682ecc14d0b68aa906ad867c3a bin/iz4 IZ4_TEST_BIN
